Rename this file to hdmi-watchdog.enable to start the HDMI CTS telemetry
monitor at boot. It is off by default because it polls every two seconds
and writes /storage/.kodi/temp/hdmi-watchdog.log for the life of the box.

  mv /storage/.config/hdmi-watchdog.enable.sample /storage/.config/hdmi-watchdog.enable
  systemctl start hdmi-watchdog

The manual tools hdmi-recover, hdmi-phy-cycle and hdmi-state-dump are always
installed and are unaffected by this file.
